                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "UniBall is a great project, really. Very simple and obvious game mechanics that creates a very dynamic competition, something like a virtual pool, where several players compete in pushing the ball into pockets (gates), colliding with their cues on the field. 1 on 1, 2 on 2, 4 on 4... or 2 on 2 on 2 on 2, for example! This game provides a great amount of variability, it runs very great, it is totally free of cost... \n\nAnd yet I click \"not recommend\". Why? Simple. It's a competitive game, but you can hardly find any players online. UniBall is a great game, but... it's dead.\n\nMaybe I just don't see the whole picture, maybe there are hundreds and thousands of dedicated players... but I looked for them and have not succeeded.",
